  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nTuesday-Sunday:\nExpecting similar conditions to persist through much of the\nforecast period, outside of low PoPs clipping the area on\nWednesday and Thursday. NWS Heat Risk continues to show the\nentire area in the Major to Extreme category through the\nupcoming weekend, therefore heat sensitive groups will need to\ntake proper precautions. Daily highs remain progged to push\ntowards middle to upper 90s, with lower 100s in portions of\nsoutheast KS into southwest MO. Likewise, daily heat index\nvalues are expected to push towards 100 to 108. As a result,\nheat headlines will likely need to be extended beyond Wednesday\nif confidence continues to increase. As mentioned though, the\none fly in the ointment would be low PoPs (< 15%) on Wednesday\nand Thursday across our northern counties. This would be the\nresult of the low chances from remnant activity sinking into the\narea, with the active jet stream displaced just north of the\narea through mid-week. If confidence continues to lean towards\nthe lower or no PoPs scenario, than heat headlines will need\nextended in time. Beyond Thursday, ensemble guidance suggest a\nrestrengthening of the upper- level ridge across the region.\nThis supports the signal for extreme heat persisting over the\nnext week or so.",
